<title>BELGIUM: Belgian 2006 OLO auctioned at average 6.653 pct.</title>
<headline>Belgian 2006 OLO auctioned at average 6.653 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Treasury gave the following details about the outcome of its monthly auction -</p>
<p>    * 7.00 pct, May 2006 OLO</p>
<p>    Avg weighted price / yield   102.377 / 6.653 pct</p>
<p>    Price range of bids	    102.200 to 102.400</p>
<p>    Stop (lowest accepted) price 102.350</p>
<p>    Percentage taken at stop     13.582</p>
<p>    Amount allotted		    5.090 billion francs</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids	    24.730 billion francs</p>
<p>* 9.00 pct, July 1998 OLO</p>
<p>    Avg weighted price / yield   109.150 / 3.950 pct</p>
<p>    Price range of bids	    109.050 to 109.150</p>
<p>    Stop (lowest accepted) price 109.150</p>
<p>    Percentage taken at stop     100</p>
<p>    Amount allotted		    3.500 billion francs</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids	    19.400 billion francs</p>
<p>* 9.00 pct, June 2001 OLO</p>
<p>    Avg weighted price / yield   114.600 / 5.469 pct</p>
<p>    Price range of bids	    114.450 to 114.600</p>
<p>    Stop (lowest accepted) price 114.600</p>
<p>    Percentage taken at stop     100</p>
<p>    Amount allotted		    8.650 billion francs</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids	    23.115 billion francs</p>
<p>NOTE - Total allocation 17.24 billion francs, down from 28.825 billion at the competitive auction in July.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6811</p>
</text>
